From aa3d092cdf3b2412fe7c7fcb638a1ddb6396200c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lmoresi <louis.moresi@anu.edu.au>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 00:07:22 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Serial custom-FMG: drop orphan coarse DOFs, do not repair
 them

Since #890 the parallel custom-FMG route builds its node transfers without
the barycentric orphan repair and drops unreached columns at install, while
the serial route still ran the repair first. Serial and parallel runs of the
same hierarchy therefore built different transfers, and iteration counts
could depend on the rank count for no reason. _reduced_transfer now uses
the parallel builds' _node_transfer_no_repair.

The repair never lowered an iteration count. It also emptied more columns
than it filled (UNFILED 63): overwriting a fine row takes away the only fine
image of that row's old coarse DOFs. On a graded finest annulus under a
uniform tail, 3,245 orphans became 8,631 empty columns, and the velocity
solve took 13 iterations against 3.

The public barycentric_prolongation default and legacy set_custom_mg keep
the repair: they have no install-time drop.

test_0894 is that fixture (velocity its <= 4; 13 on development), with a
no-orphan guard (counts 1/3/9 unchanged). Before and after, over 51 custom-MG
and placed-ribbon test files (229 tests with solves): 227 have identical
counts, with solutions within 1e-14. One is test_0894. One, test_1157's
first warm solve, takes 78 or 200 velocity iterations from run to run on the
same build. 3-D box, split ladder and K1 #893 fixtures: identical counts,
solutions within 5e-11.

Underworld development team with AI support from Claude Code
